### Last Change ###

24/10/26 : v1.1.1 - Multi-architecture image (linux/amd64 + linux/arm64), built natively per
           architecture by GitHub Actions and merged into one manifest; major.minor tags.


23/10/26 : v1.1.0 - Flood protection and web application firewall.
           * nginx limit_req/limit_conn per client IP on every host (RATE_LIMIT, RATE_BURST,
             CONN_LIMIT; rap.rate_limit, rap.rate_burst, rap.conn_limit), 429 on excess.
           * Slowloris/oversized-header hardening and HTTP/2 stream cap (conf.d/00-security.conf).
           * REAL_IP_FROM: trust X-Forwarded-For from listed proxies/CDNs.
           * ModSecurity 3.0.17 + OWASP CRS 4.30.0 compiled into the image; WAF=on|detect|off
             proxy-wide and rap.waf per host (default detect); exclusions via vhost.d/*_modsec.
           * Default X-Content-Type-Options / X-Frame-Options / Referrer-Policy headers (rap.security_headers=off).
           * Generated server blocks carry the ACME location themselves; legacy injected copies in
             vhost.d are removed on start.
           * Images published to Docker Hub (fflo/rancher-active-proxy) by GitHub Actions.


23/10/26 : v1.0.0 - Maintenance release: rebuild from source and harden.
           * rancher-gen source moved in-tree (rancher-gen/), built with Go modules; the GitLab
             artifact download that the old Dockerfile relied on no longer exists.
           * Multi-stage Dockerfile: pinned nginx:1.30-alpine, forego and rancher-gen compiled from
             pinned modules, no unverified binary downloads, OCI labels, HEALTHCHECK, nano/unzip/wget dropped.
           * Label values are validated (isHostname/isPort/isSafeToken) before being written into the
             nginx config: a service label can no longer inject nginx directives.
           * Let's Encrypt host list is plain tab-separated data parsed by letsencrypt.sh instead of a
             bash file that was `source`d (label values could execute as shell code).
           * TLS: Mozilla intermediate profile (AEAD ciphers only, no CBC/SHA1/non-PFS), http2 on,
             ssl_prefer_server_ciphers off, X25519 curves, HSTS tunable via rap.hsts.
           * Self-signed default certificate for unknown host names; server_tokens off by default;
             RFC 7919 ffdhe2048 DH group instead of a generated -dsaparam group.
           * certbot: --keep-until-expiring/--expand per cert, `certbot renew` from cron, staging<->prod
             switch handled by deleting the lineage, job lock, no placeholder e-mail, real error logging.
           * http->https redirect uses the configured host instead of the client-supplied Host header.
           * /app/remove validates its argument (no more path traversal / glob) and uses certbot delete.
           * rancher-gen: Sirupsen->sirupsen import, io/ioutil removed, two printf bugs fixed,
             RANCHER_METADATA_URL override, flag parsing moved out of init() so `go test` works.
           * GitHub Actions workflow (lint, build, smoke test, Trivy scan, weekly rebuild) replaces the
             Docker Hub hook and GitLab CI; catalog template requires a real DEFAULT_EMAIL.
           * Fixed: `rap.host=www.example.com=>8080` (port only) produced `proxy_pass 8080://...`.


